   <text type="letter">
      
      <body>
         <div type="writingSession">
            <pb n="1"/>
            <opener><dateline><date when="1943-12-22">December 22, 1943.</date><lb/>
               <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928" type="person">Professor
                  Paul Tillich</rs><lb/>
               99 Claremont Avenue<lb/>
               <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__319" type="place">New York, New York</rs><lb/>
               </dateline>
               <salute>Dear <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928" type="person">Professor
                  Tillich</rs>:</salute>
            </opener>
            <p>In January 1941, you were kind enough to make an affidavit of support for <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__4362"
                  type="person">Mrs. Annelies von Molnar</rs>. I have been retained by <rs
                  ref="#tillich_person_id__4362" type="person">Mrs. von Molnar</rs> as her attorney
               in her immigration matter, and am about to prepare the documents required by the
               State Department. <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__4362" type="person">Mrs. von Molnar</rs> would be much
               obliged if you would kindly repeat the affidavit on the new form which is now
               prescribed. In order to fill out the form, I need your answers to the questionnaire
               enclosed herewith. Please return it to me with your answers so that I can fill out
               the affidavit form and send it to you for your signature.</p>
            <p>I thank you in advance for your cooperation.</p><closer>
               <salute>Very truly yours,</salute>
               MURRAY K. JOSEPHSEN
               <lb/>By: <signed><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__4361" type="person"
                  ><hi rend="hand">Max Strauss</hi></rs></signed><lb/>
                  MS:hh<lb/>Enc.
            </closer>
         </div>
        
      </body>
   </text>
